    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py`, but it doesn't send temperature 0, so it doesn't meet your determinism requirement. The pinned `anthropic` 1.8.0 no longer accepts `temperature`, `top_k` or `top_p` in `messages.create()`. I checked the installed SDK source and none of those parameters are there.\n\nThe rest matches your spec:\n- It sends one request to `MODEL` with `max_tokens=5`.\n- The system prompt tells the model to answer with exactly one word from `LABELS`.\n- The ticket text goes in as the user message.\n- It lower-cases and strips the reply, and returns `\"question\"` if the result isn't in `LABELS`.\n\nWithout temperature, the same ticket could get different labels on different calls. The strict prompt, the 5-token limit and the fallback keep every answer one of the three labels, but they don't make it deterministic.\n\n`pytest -q` passes, but the only test checks that the labels are lower-case. Nothing exercises `label_ticket` itself, and I haven't sent a real request.\n\nDecision for you: I could force the field in with `extra_body={\"temperature\": 0}`. I haven't, because the SDK dropped the parameter on purpose. The API may well reject it or ignore it, and I haven't checked which. If you need repeatable labels, the safer fix is to cache the label for each ticket. Tell me which you want, or whether to leave it as it is."
